// madc --lsp over stdin/stdout (split arc 1C.12; design
// docs/plans/2026-10-10-lsp-in-core-design.md). The runner starts
// `madc --no-config --lsp tests/testlsp_stdio.mad` (.flags) with
// tests/testlsp_stdio.input on stdin: a Content-Length framed conversation —
// initialize, initialized, didOpen of a C document, documentSymbol, hover, a
// request no server method answers, a body that is not JSON, executeCommand
// (madc.run of an unsaved document that prints — its output comes back in
// the result, never on the protocol's stdout — and madc.check), shutdown,
// exit. This file is the FILE the server opens before any client asks.
// ORACLE: LSP 3.17 (the framing, the lifecycle, the error codes -32601 and
// -32700, exit status 0 after shutdown), clangd 18 for the answers' shapes,
// and madc -i's %run / %check on the same text.

int twice(int v)
{
    return v * 2;
}
